# Fixed 2026-09-29, defect 130's class, lane X4, on lane Y's finding.
# Symptom: a block indented deeper than anything that opens one, under a line
# that ended well, `x = 1` over a deeper `print(1) )`, was named
# `unexpected_block` and dropped whole, every mistake inside it unsaid, and
# at the top level of a file the same. Cause: the block loop named an orphan
# and dropped it, since read as lines a continuation the lexer lets through
# cost two. It is now named once and its lines read (`parse/orphans.hero`),
# their own mistakes told, a block deeper still named again, a block of arms
# read as arms, and a declaration in it told as one in any body is. One whose
# first line is the line above going on, a token that only ever goes on with
# a line, `+ 1` or `else`, or a word and then a value with no operator
# between them, `and c`, the shape of an operator another language spells as
# a word, is still the one mistake its name says, and goes whole.

use geom
    print(0) )  #~ expected_declaration expected_end_of_line

function main()
    x = 1
        print(1) )  #~ unexpected_block expected_end_of_line
        y = 2 3  #~ expected_end_of_line
    a = 2
        print(a)  #~ unexpected_block
            z = 3 )  #~ unexpected_block expected_end_of_line
    b = 3
        0 => 5  #~ unexpected_block
    c = 4
        + 1  #~ unexpected_block
    d = 5
        else  #~ unexpected_block
    e = 6
        and c  #~ unexpected_block
    f = 7
        function inner()  #~ unexpected_block expected_expression
            q = 8 )  #~ expected_end_of_line
    print(x, a, b, c, d, e, f)

# Corrected 2026-09-30 by lane recovery-b1 (defect 130's class, lane X4's
# report): the header's last sentence no longer holds. One whose first line
# is the line above going on is still named once, the one mistake its name
# says, but it no longer goes whole: the token that goes on, `else` or `and`,
# is passed over and the rest is read, so the `)` of `and c )` and a later
# line's own mistakes are told
# (`fixedbugs-130-an-orphan-that-goes-on-with-the-line-above`); `else` and
# `and c` here hold none, and this case reads the same.
